[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: Action Panoramas
UID: DOC-ACTION-PANO-001
VERSION: 1.0
DATE: 2026-09-26

[GRAMMAR]
ELEMENTS:
- TAG: REQUIREMENT
  FIELDS:
  - TITLE: UID
    TYPE: String
    REQUIRED: True
  - TITLE: TITLE
    TYPE: String
    REQUIRED: True
  - TITLE: STATEMENT
    TYPE: String
    REQUIRED: True
  - TITLE: RATIONALE
    TYPE: String
    REQUIRED: False
  - TITLE: COMMENT
    TYPE: String
    REQUIRED: False
  - TITLE: PRIORITY
    TYPE: String
    REQUIRED: False
  - TITLE: STATUS
    TYPE: String
    REQUIRED: False

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: AP-001
TITLE: Uniform Frame Marker
STATEMENT: Sportball SHALL score each decoded photo on a fixed-size grayscale thumbnail by its mean gray level and the variance of pixels around that mean. A run of at least a configurable count of consecutive frames whose variance is at or below a configurable score SHALL be a known-panorama marker. The default count SHALL be 2 and the default variance SHALL be 100. A marker MAY be a covered lens, a frame of sky, or a zoomed frame of ground.
RATIONALE: The photographer marks the end of a pan with a nearly uniform frame. Variance around the grayscale mean accepts black, sky, and ground alike, and stays independent of file resolution.
PRIORITY: High
STATUS: Implemented

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: AP-002
TITLE: Known Panorama Walk-Back
STATEMENT: From the frame immediately before a uniform-frame marker, Sportball SHALL walk backward while each gap is at most a configurable discontinuity (default 10 seconds). Inside that window it SHALL run cpfind and cut the panorama at a configurable weak-link rule. The default rule SHALL cut at the weak link with the largest time gap, breaking ties toward the marker frames. A link SHALL be weak when its control-point count is at most a configurable split threshold (default 0). The whole window SHALL be kept when no link is weak.
RATIONALE: The pan just finished is the suffix before the uniform pair. A long gap with no overlap is the start of that pan. A gap over 10 seconds is a different shot.
PRIORITY: High
STATUS: Implemented

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: AP-003
TITLE: Guessed Panorama Geometry
STATEMENT: Sportball SHALL also search unmarked bursts. A guessed panorama SHALL be a run of at least max(min-frames, stride+1) frames where every neighboring pair has at least a configurable overlap count (default 10) and every pair stride frames apart has at most a configurable far count (default 0). The default stride SHALL be 3 and the default minimum SHALL be 5. A run whose neighbors overlap and whose stride pairs also overlap SHALL be reported and SHALL NOT be written. Frames already claimed by a known panorama SHALL NOT be searched again.
RATIONALE: An action panorama moves far enough that frame N does not overlap frame N±3, while adjacent frames still overlap enough to stitch. Duration alone does not define the pan.
PRIORITY: High
STATUS: Implemented

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: AP-004
TITLE: Discontinuous Shots
STATEMENT: Two photos separated by more than the discontinuity threshold SHALL NOT be placed in the same panorama. The default threshold SHALL be 10 seconds.
RATIONALE: A gap that long is two shots, whether or not the framing could theoretically overlap.
PRIORITY: High
STATUS: Implemented

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: AP-005
TITLE: Hugin Project Output
STATEMENT: Each accepted panorama SHALL be written as a folder of symlinks (or copies when requested) plus one Hugin .pto project inside that folder. Uniform marker frames SHALL NOT be placed in the folder. Folder names SHALL be known_pano or guessed_pano, numbered together in capture order, with the same date and time suffix pattern as game folders. The .pto SHALL reference those folder entries. Control points SHALL be detected on previews and scaled to full resolution. Sportball SHALL NOT mask or crop images inside the Hugin project, and SHALL NOT write per-image sidecar documents.
RATIONALE: The photographer includes and excludes regions in Hugin. The .pto is the stitch project, not a metadata sidecar.
PRIORITY: High
STATUS: Implemented

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: AP-006
TITLE: cpfind Required
STATEMENT: When control points are required, Sportball SHALL run pto_gen and cpfind from PATH. If either tool is missing it SHALL raise RuntimeError and name the hugin-tools package.
RATIONALE: Overlap is measured by Hugin control points. There is no silent fallback that pretends frames overlap.
PRIORITY: High
STATUS: Implemented

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: AP-007
TITLE: Dry Run
STATEMENT: A dry run SHALL print each decoded photo's grayscale mean and variance, each uniform-frame marker, and the control-point count of each link in every accepted or rejected run. It SHALL NOT create panorama folders.
RATIONALE: The variance and overlap thresholds are tuned on a real game before anything is written.
PRIORITY: Medium
STATUS: Implemented

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: AP-008
TITLE: Positions and View
STATEMENT: Every written Hugin project SHALL be optimized for yaw, pitch, roll, and horizontal field of view (y, p, r, v) and SHALL NOT optimize distortion, exposure, white balance, or vignetting in that pass. The position anchor and the exposure anchor SHALL both be the median image. For an odd count that is the middle photo. For an even count that is the earlier of the two middle photos, so 5 photos use the 3rd and 4 photos use the 2nd.
RATIONALE: The first Hugin pass is the Positions and View preset. One reference frame keeps the pan from drifting in position or exposure.
PRIORITY: High
STATUS: Implemented

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: AP-009
TITLE: Inline Stitch
STATEMENT: Stitching SHALL be on by default. After all panorama folders have been written, Sportball SHALL run hugin_executor --stitching on each optimized project, one after another, and SHALL NOT open PTBatcherGUI. The stitched image SHALL be a JPEG named like the project, in that panorama folder. ``--no-stitch`` SHALL skip stitching. The JPEG SHALL exist before the cropped copy is written. A project that hugin_executor cannot stitch SHALL be reported and skipped, the remaining projects SHALL still be stitched and cropped, and the skipped folder and its .pto SHALL be kept. A missing hugin_executor SHALL still stop the command.
RATIONALE: An inline JPEG stitch needs no batch window and leaves an image for the crop in the same run. The command works headless. One pan that Hugin rejects does not cost the rest of the game its panoramas.
PRIORITY: Medium
STATUS: Implemented

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: AP-010
TITLE: Per-Input Panorama Folder
STATEMENT: Each input directory SHALL receive its own panorama directory, a sibling whose name is the input directory name plus -panos. Five input directories SHALL produce five -panos directories. Panoramas from one input SHALL stay in that input's sibling and SHALL NOT be written into a shared output directory. Numbering SHALL restart in each sibling. A directory that is the -panos sibling of another selected input SHALL NOT be scanned. A dry run SHALL NOT create those sibling directories.
RATIONALE: Panoramas stay next to the game folder they came from. A shared dump folder separates them from that source.
PRIORITY: High
STATUS: Implemented

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: AP-011
TITLE: Cropped Stitch
STATEMENT: Cropping SHALL be on by default and SHALL be pure Python. After the panorama directory exists, Sportball SHALL write one <pano_name>_cropped.jpg for each stitched panorama it finds there, in the same folder as that stitched image. The crop box SHALL be the bounding box of pixels that are not black canvas. The full stitch SHALL be left in place. --no-crop SHALL skip that file. A dry run SHALL NOT write it. A frame that is entirely black SHALL NOT produce a cropped file. A file already named _cropped SHALL NOT be cropped again.
RATIONALE: The full stitch shows the black canvas and whether the edges can be cleaned up by hand. The cropped file is the picture without that canvas.
PRIORITY: High
STATUS: Implemented
